    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0911" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/8–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-22T19:00:00-04:00">August 22, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7147. For Taylor<anchor n="8" xml:id="d310-f1"/> from Treasury. Urtel 6615 June
                        30.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d310-f2"/> Dept and Treasury bothered by apparent
                    relaxation Brit controls over Swiss accounts and feel such action may be
                    premature at this time. It is our feeling that in view of defects Swiss controls
                    and general reluctance of Swiss to cooperate fully on <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Safehaven</hi> both we and Brit should hesitate
                    before relaxing our controls over Swiss accounts.</p>
                <p>Discuss with Brit desirability of maintaining existing controls over Swiss
                    assets, at least until some indication is recd of Swiss compliance on <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Safehaven</hi> program. You should point out to Brit
                    steps we are taking to hold up on certification procedure, and since they are
                    committed with us to obtain fullest <hi rendition="#small-caps">Safehaven</hi>
                    results from Swiss, <pb facs="0912" n="900" xml:id="pg900"/> they should
                    likewise be exceedingly reluctant to remove restrictions from Swiss assets. You
                    might add we have found Swiss extremely sensitive to our suggestions if they
                    feel their assets in this country are in any way prejudiced, and probably Allied
                    control of Swiss assets is the most potent weapon we have with which to obtain
                    Swiss compliance on <hi rendition="#small-caps">Safehaven</hi>.</p>
                <p>Report results of discussions. [Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="8" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably William H. Taylor, Assistant Director, Division of Monetary Research,
                    Treasury Department, assigned to London as U.S. Treasury Representative.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d310-f2" n="9" xml:id="d310-f2-content">
